{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:17:09.424Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"tool","toolName":"read_files","toolCallId":"toolu_01Pw1e8sdWNRQHD1JJsy5Ewb","output":[{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\NEXT.md","result":" 1 | # NEXT TASK: T2, main flow end to end (API + UI)\n 2 | \n 3 | T1 reviewed: 93/93 tests pass and typecheck is clean. Answers to your requests:\n 4 | 1. External checks are needs_verification but don't block ready_for_review on their own: **approved** (show them as a visible \"check at the bank\" list under the readiness banner).\n 5 | 2. Land in a spouse's or minor child's name → owner-name mismatch becomes needs_verification: **approved**.\n 6 | 3. Orunodoi any-of list and the widow BPL-proof document stay provisional: **approved**.\n 7 | \n 8 | Note: `.env.local` does NOT exist yet (Das will add `CLINE_API_KEY` and `CLINE_MODEL`). So:\n 9 | - `ai.ts` must handle a missing key gracefully: return `{ error: \"ai_unavailable\" }` and the UI falls back to manual entry. No crash, and no build failure.\n10 | - Tests mock `ai.ts`; no network in tests.\n11 | \n12 | Do `tasks/backlog/T2-main-flow.md`. Adjustments:\n13 | - `src/core/samples.ts` already exists from T1; reuse it, don't duplicate.\n14 | - Default language Assamese, English toggle; keep all fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts` (reuse `src/core/labels.ts` where it fits).\n15 | - The report screen shows: the Eligibility banner, the Readiness banner, then \"Fix before you apply\" (action_required), then \"Please verify\" (needs_verification, including external checks), then \"OK\" (collapsed). Each item shows where to fix it, a source link and \"verified on\" date, and a \"provisional rule\" badge where relevant. Benefit amount: central share and state top-up shown separately (\"state top-up: confirm locally\" when null).\n16 | - Add a clear \"Demo mode: fake sample documents\" label when a sample is used.\n17 | \n18 | **Done when:** everything in T2's \"Done when\" holds; `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm run build` all pass; LOG.md updated; committed \"T2: main flow\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\activeContext.md","result":" 1 | # Active context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Current state\n 4 | T1 (core rule engine v2) is done. `src/core/` has the zod schemas, the 3 rule packs with provenance, the registry, name matcher, age, Aadhaar masking, benefit overrides, rule engine, rejection codes and fake sample sets A/B/C. 93 tests pass; typecheck, lint and build are clean.\n 5 | The app is still a placeholder home page, now titled \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\" with \"Check before you apply\" / \"আবেদনৰ আগতে পৰীক্ষা কৰক\", `<html lang=\"as\">`.\n 6 | \n 7 | ## Decisions made in T1\n 8 | - Brief v2: **Assamese default + English**; two verdicts (eligibility, readiness); provenance on every rule (verified vs provisional).\n 9 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable, but a `verified` rule must have one (schema refine). Provisional overrides from the T3 agent can start with `sourceUrl: null`.\n10 | - `ExtractedDoc.fields` is strict and only holds `aadhaarLast4` (never a full Aadhaar number). A missing per-field confidence means \"entered/confirmed by the user\"; < 0.8 → needs_verification.\n11 | - The name reference document is Aadhaar for PM-KISAN and the widow pension, and the ration card for Orunodoi.\n12 | - A PM-KISAN land-owner mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (not ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes (farmer family = spouse/minor children).\n13 | - Orunodoi question ids: `nfsa_enrolled` (requirement); any-of `widow | person_with_disability | aay_card | income_below_2_lakh`; exclusions `elected_representative | professional | govt_staff_or_pensioner | contractor_or_trader | large_landholder | four_wheeler | similar_state_scheme`. All provisional.\n14 | - Widow pension: all mandatory docs (incl. `bpl_proof`) are provisional (\"commonly required; confirm locally\"); age and BPL are verified.\n15 | - The registry is in-memory: `registerScheme` validates, rejects a duplicate id+version and keeps old versions. T3 will persist versions in SQLite and register them at startup.\n16 | - Assamese strings in `labels.ts`, the scheme packs and `rejectionCodes.ts` are drafts awaiting native-speaker review (Das).\n17 | \n18 | ## Next step\n19 | T2: main flow (scheme picker → documents/samples → confirm fields → questions → two-verdict report), `src/i18n.ts` (as/en), AI gateway `src/server/ai.ts`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\productContext.md","result":" 1 | # Product context: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Why it exists\n 4 | Eligible people lose welfare benefits *after* applying: names that don't match across Aadhaar, bank and land records; Aadhaar not seeded to the bank; missing certificates; rejection reasons they cannot understand. Documented example: Rajasthan 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the 3rd instalment, mostly because of Aadhaar name mismatches (sources in `docs/research.md`).\n 5 | \n 6 | KaagazCheck checks the papers **before** the person applies, in **Assamese (default) with an English toggle**, and says exactly what to fix and where.\n 7 | **Promise:** we help catch preventable mistakes. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam (farmer, widow, woman of a household) on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current with the Rule Maintenance Agent (Cline SDK).\n12 | \n13 | ## Schemes in scope (rule packs v2, `docs/schemes.md` is the source of truth)\n14 | - **PM-KISAN** (`pm-kisan`): flagship end-to-end demo. No landholding-size limit.\n15 | - **Orunodoi 3.0, Assam** (`orunodoi-3`): only the ration card and ₹1,250/month are verified; everything else is provisional → \"needs verification\".\n16 | - **Widow Pension IGNWPS** (`nsap-widow`): age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month; state top-up unconfirmed.\n17 | \n18 | ## Main demo path (3 minutes)\n19 | 1. Pick a scheme.\n20 | 2. Add documents: photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\" (A clean PM-KISAN, B name mismatch, C widow missing death certificate).\n21 | 3. AI reads each document → fields + confidence; low confidence → the user confirms or edits.\n22 | 4. Answer the yes/no questions.\n23 | 5. Rule engine → **two verdicts**: *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification). Each check has a reason, where to fix it, and its source (provenance, verified vs provisional).\n24 | 6. Assamese report + printable cover sheet.\n25 | \n26 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n27 | A scheme notice → the agent proposes a rule change (new scheme or new version, with provenance) → writes regression tests → runs them through the engine → diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme), `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (one-time ₹1,500 for October 2026, via a time-bounded benefit override).\n28 | \n29 | ## Second mode (T4)\n30 | Rejection decoder: rejection text → known reason code (`src/core/rejectionCodes.ts`) → fix steps in Assamese + English.\n31 | \n32 | ## Trust rules\n33 | - The AI only reads and explains; the rule engine decides.\n34 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional rules and external facts (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified) → needs_verification, never a definitive pass/fail.\n35 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity: only an exact (normalised) match is `ok`.\n36 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n37 | - Demo uses fake sample documents only. AI-generated Assamese is labelled \"draft\"; fixed Assamese strings need native-speaker review.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\progress.md","result":" 1 | # Progress\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Done\n 4 | - [x] T0: Memory Bank, Next.js 16 scaffold (TS strict, Tailwind v4, ESLint), Vitest + fast-check + zod, npm scripts, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`, placeholder page, smoke test, first commit.\n 5 | - [x] T1: core rule engine v2. Step 0 (memory bank refreshed for brief v2; title \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", taglines EN/AS, `<html lang=\"as\">`); zod types; 3 rule packs with provenance + versioned registry; name matcher (Devanagari + Assamese/Bengali transliteration, Jaro-Winkler); `ageOn`; `maskAadhaar`; `benefitOn` with overrides; `evaluate` with two verdicts; rejection codes EN/AS; samples A/B/C. 93 tests.\n 6 | \n 7 | ## To do\n 8 | - [ ] T2: main flow (scheme picker → documents/samples → confirm fields → questions → two-verdict report, Assamese/English via `src/i18n.ts`, AI gateway `src/server/ai.ts`)\n 9 | - [ ] T3: Rule Maintenance Agent (`@cline/sdk`, `node:sqlite` `rule_versions`, tests + human approval, versioned packs)\n10 | - [ ] T4: rejection decoder + polish\n11 | - [ ] T-last: freeze, full README, demo path check\n12 | \n13 | ## Known issues\n14 | - `npm install` warns that eslint@9 is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0). Harmless.\n15 | - Assamese strings are drafts; they need native-speaker review before the demo.\n16 | - The transliteration table is basic (good enough for possible_match on common names; cross-script is never `same`).","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\projectbrief.md","result":" 1 | # Project brief v2: KaagazCheck (কাগজ চেক): \"Check before you apply\"\n 2 | \n 3 | **Pitch:** We help citizens catch preventable welfare-application mistakes *before* they submit their papers. Our AI reads the documents; a tested rule engine checks them; and Cline maintains the rules as official guidelines change.\n 4 | **Promise:** we reduce preventable errors. We do NOT guarantee approval; the department decides.\n 5 | \n 6 | ## Problem (evidence: docs/research.md)\n 7 | Eligible people lose benefits after applying because their documents disagree (name spellings across Aadhaar, bank and land record; account not Aadhaar-seeded; missing papers) or because rejections arrive unexplained. In Rajasthan in 2019, only about 23% of registered PM-KISAN farmers got the third instalment, mostly due to name mismatches with Aadhaar.\n 8 | \n 9 | ## Users\n10 | - **Citizen** in Assam on a basic Android phone, often helped by family or a CSC/NGO helper.\n11 | - **Rule maintainer** (helper organisation) who keeps scheme rules current using the Cline agent.\n12 | \n13 | ## Languages\n14 | **Assamese (default) + English toggle.** All fixed UI and check messages live in one `src/i18n.ts` with `as` and `en` keys. Assamese strings must be reviewed by a native speaker before the demo (Das will arrange). AI-generated Assamese (letters, explanations) is labelled \"draft\".\n15 | \n16 | ## Scope: rule packs v2 (docs/schemes.md is the source of truth)\n17 | - **PM-KISAN: flagship, full end-to-end demo** (name mismatch, missing document, uncertain bank status).\n18 | - **Orunodoi 3.0: Assam relevance, verified rules only;** provisional criteria → \"needs verification\".\n19 | - **Widow Pension (IGNWPS): simple, reliable rules** (age 40–79, BPL, central ₹300/month).\n20 | \n21 | ## Architecture (the trust design)\n22 | 1. **Document reader (AI):** extracts names, dates, account details and document type, with per-field confidence. Low confidence → user confirms.\n23 | 2. **Deterministic rule engine (pure code, tested):** normalises fields, checks consistency, evaluates verified criteria, finds missing documents. Provisional rules and external facts → `needs_verification`.\n24 | 3. **Two separate verdicts:** *Eligibility* (likely_eligible / not_eligible / needs_verification) and *Readiness* (ready_for_review / action_required / needs_verification).\n25 | 4. **Next steps:** corrections, where to go (bank, Aadhaar centre, circle office, Gram Panchayat), the source of each rule, and a printable cover sheet.\n26 | 5. **Explainer (AI, optional):** friendly wording in Assamese, built only from the engine's result.\n27 | \n28 | ## Core loop (must-ship demo path)\n29 | Pick scheme → add documents (photo, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm low-confidence fields → answer yes/no questions → two-verdict report with fixes and sources → print cover sheet.\n30 | Samples (clearly fake): A = clean PM-KISAN farmer → ready_for_review (+ bank seeding needs verification). B = PM-KISAN with \"RAMESH KR SHARMA\" (bank, possible match) and \"Rameshwar Sharma\" (land record, mismatch) → action_required. C = widow pension, missing death certificate → action_required.\n31 | \n32 | ## Cline inside the product: Rule Maintenance Agent (T3)\n33 | Upload or paste a scheme notice → a `@cline/sdk` Agent proposes a **rule change** (new scheme or edited rule, with provenance: sourceUrl, clause, effectiveDate) → writes **regression tests** → runs them through the engine (existing scheme tests must still pass) → shows a diff + test results → a **human approves** → a new rule-pack version is published (old version kept). Demo inputs: `docs/sample-guideline-ignoaps.md` (add a scheme) and `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` (a one-time payment change, to show versioning).\n34 | \n35 | ## Trust rules (non-negotiable)\n36 | - AI reads and explains; **code decides**. No eligibility claim from model text.\n37 | - Aadhaar masked to the last 4 digits everywhere; images processed in memory, never stored.\n38 | - Every rule carries provenance; provisional → needs_verification.\n39 | - A fuzzy name score never equals identity.\n40 | - Demo uses fake documents only.\n41 | \n42 | ## Data model sketch\n43 | - `RuleProvenance` { sourceUrl, sourceTitle, clause?, effectiveDate?, verifiedOn, version, status: verified | provisional }\n44 | - `SchemeRule` { id, version, nameEn, nameAs, benefit { centralShare, stateTopUp|null, period, effectiveDate, provenance }, mandatoryDocs[], supportingDocs[], ageRange?, eligibilityAnyOf[], exclusions[], externalChecks[], each criterion with provenance }\n45 | - `ExtractedDoc` { docType, fields { name, dob, aadhaarLast4, accountNo, ifsc, ownerNames[], husbandName, ... }, confidence per field }\n46 | - `Report` { eligibility, readiness, checks[], schemeVersion, asOfDate }\n47 | - DB (T3): `rule_versions` { schemeId, version, ruleJson, testsJson, testResultJson, status: proposed | published | rejected, sourceNote, createdAt, approvedAt }\n48 | \n49 | ## Stretch\n50 | Assamese voice readout (only if the browser has an as-IN voice; otherwise hide) · rejection-notice decoder (T4) · helper mode for many applicants.\n51 | \n52 | ## Cut list (cut in this order)\n53 | Voice → decoder letter drafting → real photo upload (keep samples + manual entry) → cover-sheet styling. **Never cut:** the two-verdict report, provenance, the Cline agent with tests + approval.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\README.md","result":"1 | # Memory Bank\n2 | Empty until the problem statement is released. In task T0, Cline creates:\n3 | `projectbrief.md` (from Claude's brief), `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md`.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\systemPatterns.md","result":" 1 | # System patterns\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Core pipeline: AI reads → rule engine decides → AI explains\n 4 | 1. **Read (AI):** a document image or text → `ExtractedDoc` (fields + per-field confidence), validated with zod.\n 5 | 2. **Decide (pure code):** `evaluate(scheme, docs, answers, asOfDate) → Report` in `src/core/evaluate.ts`. Deterministic, unit- and property-tested. No model text ever decides a status.\n 6 | 3. **Explain (AI, optional):** friendlier Assamese wording or a letter draft, built only from the report's checks (labelled \"draft\").\n 7 | \n 8 | ## Module boundaries\n 9 | - `src/core/`: pure TypeScript. No React, network, DB, `process.env` or implicit \"today\" (`asOfDate` is always passed in).\n10 |   - `types.ts` zod schemas: `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (versioned), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n11 |   - `schemes/` rule packs (`pm-kisan.ts`, `orunodoi-3.ts`, `nsap-widow.ts`; provenance helpers in `sources.ts`) + registry `index.ts`: `getScheme(id, version?)`, `listSchemes()`, `listSchemeVersions(id)`, `registerScheme(rule)` (validates; keeps old versions; newest wins), `questionsFor(scheme)`.\n12 |   - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`), `age.ts` (`ageOn`), `aadhaar.ts` (`maskAadhaar`), `benefit.ts` (`benefitOn` with time-bounded overrides), `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts` (bilingual doc/office labels, disclaimer), `samples.ts` (fake sample sets A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n13 | - `src/server/ai.ts` (T2): the **only** module that calls a model. Structured JSON → zod → one retry → safe fallback. Logs model, prompt version, input hash (never raw personal data).\n14 | - `src/server/store.ts` (T3): the **only** database writer (`node:sqlite`, WAL, transactions); `rule_versions` table.\n15 | - `src/server/agent/` (T3): `@cline/sdk` Rule Maintenance Agent; its tools call `src/core` (`registerScheme`, `evaluate`).\n16 | - `src/app/api/**/route.ts`: thin handlers with `export const runtime = \"nodejs\"`.\n17 | - `src/app/**`: UI (Assamese default, English toggle; fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts` from T2). Calls API routes, never the model.\n18 | \n19 | ## Result model (docs/schemes.md v2)\n20 | - Check result: `ok | action_required | needs_verification | not_applicable`; kind: `document | name | field | eligibility | external`. Every check has `messageEn`, `messageAs`, `fixWhere`, `provenance`, plus `match` for name checks.\n21 | - **Eligibility:** `not_eligible` only when a **verified** eligibility criterion failed; any provisional, unanswered or unreadable criterion → `needs_verification`; else `likely_eligible`.\n22 | - **Readiness:** any `action_required` (missing mandatory doc, name `mismatch`, bad IFSC/account format, failed verified criterion) → `action_required`; else any non-external `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence, provisional) → `needs_verification`; else `ready_for_review`. External checks (bank seeding, account active, eKYC, land verified, ration card active) are always `needs_verification` and listed, but on their own they don't block `ready_for_review`.\n23 | - Money: `centralShare` + `stateTopUp` (null = unconfirmed → `total` null; never show an unconfirmed total). Overrides are inclusive date windows; the last matching one wins.\n24 | \n25 | ## Name matching (showcase, defensive)\n26 | Tokenise → drop leading honorifics (SHRI/SMT/MR/MRS/KUMARI/LATE…) → transliterate Devanagari/Assamese/Bengali → canonical variants (KR→KUMAR, MD/MOHD→MOHAMMAD, DEBI→DEVI, SK→SHEIKH…). Levels: `same` (identical after formatting; the only level that gives `ok`), `possible_match` (variants, transliteration, word order, or every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85), `initials_only`, `mismatch` (incl. a missing/extra word). The score is shown but never decides.\n27 | \n28 | ## Privacy\n29 | Aadhaar: only `aadhaarLast4` is stored in `ExtractedDoc`; `maskAadhaar` → `XXXX XXXX 1234`. Images processed in memory only. Minimum personal data.\n30 | \n31 | ## Testing\n32 | Vitest + fast-check, tests first for core logic. Properties: name same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never `ok`, Orunodoi never `not_eligible`, evaluate deterministic + schema-valid, readiness invariant.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\memory-bank\\techContext.md","result":" 1 | # Tech context\n 2 | \n 3 | ## Stack\n 4 | - One Next.js 16 app (App Router, `src/` dir, `@/*` → `./src/*`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`).\n 5 | - Validation: zod 4.\n 6 | - Tests: Vitest 5 (Node environment, `src/**/*.test.ts`) + fast-check 4.\n 7 | - Lint: ESLint 9 flat config (`eslint-config-next`); `next lint` no longer exists in Next 16.\n 8 | - Database (T3): built-in `node:sqlite` (WAL); fall back to `better-sqlite3` only if needed. `node:sqlite` loads on this machine.\n 9 | - AI: Cline API (OpenAI-compatible), base URL `https://api.cline.bot/api/v1`, all calls via `src/server/ai.ts`.\n10 | - In-product agent (T3): `@cline/sdk` `Agent`, `providerId: \"openai-compatible\"`, tools via `createTool` with zod schemas.\n11 | \n12 | ## Environment\n13 | - Windows, PowerShell 5.1; the path contains a space (`C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build`). Use npm scripts and cross-platform Node code.\n14 | - Node v24.21.0, npm 11.19.0, git 2.55.0.\n15 | - Secrets only in `.env.local` (git-ignored): `CLINE_API_KEY`, `CLINE_MODEL` (e.g. `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5`, never a `:batch` model). The template is `.env.example`.\n16 | - Write files containing Assamese (or other non-Latin text) with the editor tool (UTF-8), not PowerShell redirection. Assamese uses ৰ (U+09F0) and ৱ (U+09F1), not Bengali র/ব.\n17 | - The editor tool rejects payloads over ~6000 characters: write large files in chunks (create, then insert at the end).\n18 | - `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so never leave scratch `.ts` files in the repo root while running `next build`.\n19 | \n20 | ## npm scripts\n21 | | Script | Command |\n22 | |---|---|\n23 | | `dev` | `next dev` |\n24 | | `build` | `next build` |\n25 | | `start` | `next start` |\n26 | | `lint` | `eslint .` |\n27 | | `typecheck` | `tsc --noEmit` |\n28 | | `test` | `vitest run` |\n29 | | `test:watch` | `vitest` |\n30 | \n31 | ## Gotchas found in T0\n32 | - Vitest 5 needs `@types/node` ≥ 22 (peer dep), so `@types/node` is `^22`.\n33 | - The Vitest config is `vitest.config.mts` (ESM); a `.ts` config triggers a Vite \"configLoader native\" warning because `package.json` has no `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n34 | - The global `LayoutProps<\"/\">` type only exists after `next build`/`next dev` generate `.next/types`, so `layout.tsx` uses an explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` to keep `npm run typecheck` working on a clean checkout.\n35 | - Vite writes warnings to stderr, which PowerShell reports as `NativeCommandError`. Check the real exit code (e.g. run via `cmd /c ... & echo %ERRORLEVEL%`).\n36 | - `npm install` is slow here (about 5 minutes for a fresh install); long commands can exceed the tool timeout, so run them in the background with logs.\n37 | \n38 | ## Scaffold notes\n39 | Generated with `create-next-app@16.4.0` in a temp folder and copied in (it refuses non-empty folders). Defaults kept: `cacheComponents: true`, `partialPrefetching: true`. `AGENTS.md` is written by Next (`next dev` re-adds it), so it is committed.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\LOG.md","result":" 1 | # Build log (Cline appends after every task)\n 2 | \n 3 | ## T0: scaffold + memory bank (run-133358-c1ef, 2026-10-10)\n 4 | Followed the plan from run-133031-4cma.\n 5 | \n 6 | **Files created/changed**\n 7 | - Memory Bank: `memory-bank/productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `techContext.md`, `activeContext.md`, `progress.md` (`projectbrief.md` untouched).\n 8 | - Scaffold (create-next-app@16.4.0 in a temp folder, copied in): `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `tsconfig.json` (strict), `next.config.ts`, `eslint.config.mjs` (+ ignores for `.cline-runs/`, `docs/`, `memory-bank/`, `tasks/`), `next-env.d.ts`, `AGENTS.md`, `public/*`, `src/app/{layout.tsx,page.tsx,globals.css,favicon.ico}`.\n 9 | - New: `src/core/appInfo.ts` (title/taglines, pure), `src/core/appInfo.test.ts` (smoke test, also exercises zod + fast-check), `vitest.config.mts`, `.env.example` (`CLINE_API_KEY=`, `CLINE_MODEL=`), `README.md` (short placeholder), `.gitignore` (ignores `.env`, `.env*.local`, `node_modules`, `.next`, `*.db*`; keeps `.env.example` and `.cline-runs/`).\n10 | - Deps added: `zod@^4.6.5`, dev `vitest@^5.0.3`, `fast-check@^4.10.2`, `@types/node@^22`.\n11 | - Scripts: `dev`, `build`, `start`, `lint` (`eslint .`), `typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`), `test` (`vitest run`), `test:watch`.\n12 | \n13 | **Results**\n14 | - `npm test`: 1 file, 3 passed, 0 failed.\n15 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass (0 problems). `npm run build`: pass (Next 16.4.0, Turbopack; `/` prerendered static).\n16 | - Verified the built HTML contains \"KaagazCheck: कागज़ चेक\" and `lang=\"hi\"`, and the CSS contains the Tailwind utilities used.\n17 | \n18 | **Deviations from the plan**\n19 | - `@types/node` bumped from `^20` to `^22` (Vitest 5 peer requirement; matches Node 22+).\n20 | - Vitest config is `.mts` instead of `.ts` (avoids a Vite ESM/CJS config warning).\n21 | - `layout.tsx` uses explicit `Readonly<{ children: React.ReactNode }>` instead of the generated global `LayoutProps<\"/\">`, so `typecheck` passes before `.next/types` exists.\n22 | - No `postcss.config.mjs`: create-next-app 16.4 wires Tailwind v4 via the `@tailwindcss/turbopack` loader in `next.config.ts`; Tailwind confirmed working in the build.\n23 | \n24 | **Open issues**\n25 | - npm warns `eslint@9` is deprecated (pinned by eslint-config-next 16.4.0) and that `unrs-resolver` has an unapproved postinstall script; neither blocks lint or build.\n26 | - `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` appeared in `docs/` during this run (not created by Cline); committed as-is with `git add -A`.\n27 | \n28 | **Requests for Claude**\n29 | - None blocking. Please confirm that `docs/sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md` is intended for T4 (rejection decoder) and reference it in the task spec if so.\n30 | \n31 | ## T1: core rule engine v2 (run-134715-f3yl, 2026-10-10)\n32 | Followed `tasks/NEXT.md` (Step 0 + `tasks/backlog/T1-core-engine.md`), with `docs/schemes.md` v2 as the source of truth. I wrote the tests first: all new test files were written before the implementations, and the Step 0 smoke tests failed until `appInfo.ts` was updated.\n33 | \n34 | **Step 0**\n35 | - Memory bank: `productContext.md`, `systemPatterns.md`, `activeContext.md` rewritten for brief v2 (two verdicts, provenance, Assamese). `progress.md` and `techContext.md` updated.\n36 | - `src/core/appInfo.ts`: `APP_TITLE` \"KaagazCheck: কাগজ চেক\", `APP_TAGLINE_EN` \"Check before you apply\", `APP_TAGLINE_AS` \"আবেদনৰ আগতে পৰীক্ষা কৰক\", `APP_LANG = \"as\"`, and a longer `APP_DESCRIPTION_EN` for meta. `layout.tsx` uses `lang={APP_LANG}`; `page.tsx` shows the Assamese tagline first. The smoke test checks the exact title and taglines, Assamese ৰ (U+09F0) rather than Bengali র, and `lang`.\n37 | \n38 | **Files created (all pure, in `src/core/`)**\n39 | - `types.ts`: zod schemas `RuleProvenance`, `SchemeRule` (with `version`), `ExtractedDoc`, `Answers`, `Question`, `DocRequirement`, `NameCheckRule`, `FieldCheckRule`, `ExternalCheckRule`, `AgeRange`, `Benefit` (+ `BenefitOverride`), `Check`, `Report`, `BenefitOn`.\n40 | - `schemes/sources.ts` (provenance builders, verifiedOn 2026-10-10), `schemes/pm-kisan.ts`, `schemes/orunodoi-3.ts`, `schemes/nsap-widow.ts`, `schemes/index.ts` (`getScheme`, `listSchemes`, `listSchemeVersions`, `registerScheme`, `questionsFor`).\n41 | - `nameMatch.ts` (+ `transliterate.ts`: Devanagari and Assamese/Bengali → Latin), `age.ts`, `aadhaar.ts`, `benefit.ts`, `evaluate.ts`, `rejectionCodes.ts`, `labels.ts`, `samples.ts` (fake samples A/B/C), `dates.ts`.\n42 | - Tests: `nameMatch.test.ts`, `age.test.ts`, `aadhaar.test.ts`, `benefit.test.ts`, `evaluate.test.ts`, `rejectionCodes.test.ts`, `schemes/schemes.test.ts`.\n43 | \n44 | **Results**\n45 | - `npm test`: 8 files, **93 passed, 0 failed** (including fast-check properties: same-as-itself, symmetry, mask ≤ 4 digits, possible_match never ok, Orunodoi never not_eligible, deterministic + schema-valid report, readiness invariant).\n46 | - `npm run typecheck`: pass. `npm run lint`: pass. `npm run build`: pass. The built HTML has `lang=\"as\"`, the Assamese title and both taglines, and no Devanagari.\n47 | - Required name cases and their scores: same (1) / same (1) / possible_match (0.999) / possible_match (0.999) / initials_only (0.875) / mismatch (0.644) / mismatch (0.778).\n48 | - Samples on 2026-10-10: A → likely_eligible + ready_for_review (4 external checks need verification). B → action_required (bank possible_match, land mismatch). C → action_required (death certificate missing).\n49 | \n50 | **Design decisions / interpretations (please review)**\n51 | - **Readiness with external checks:** external checks are always `needs_verification` but do not by themselves stop `ready_for_review`. This is needed for the T1 spec \"clean → ready_for_review with bank seeding as needs_verification\". Any other `needs_verification` (possible match, initials, low confidence < 0.8, provisional criterion, unanswered question) → readiness `needs_verification`.\n52 | - **A verified criterion that fails** (e.g. income tax payer) → eligibility `not_eligible` and readiness `action_required`.\n53 | - **Name `same`** means identical after formatting (case, punctuation, spaces, joined words, leading honorifics), compared in the original script. Any cross-script comparison is at best `possible_match`. The score is capped at 0.999 for anything that is not `same`. `possible_match` also covers reordered words and \"every word pair Jaro-Winkler ≥ 0.85\". A missing or extra word is a `mismatch` (so \"Rameshwar Sharma\" vs \"Ramesh Kumar Sharma\" is a mismatch).\n54 | - **Honorifics** are dropped only when they lead the name, so \"Sunita Kumari\" keeps KUMARI as a surname.\n55 | - **PM-KISAN land owner:** a mismatch becomes `needs_verification` (never ok) if the user answers `land_in_family_member_name` = yes. docs/schemes.md allows \"applicant (or a family member) as owner\". The relationship can't be proven from a photo.\n56 | - **Orunodoi** name checks use the ration card as the reference. Provisional questions are `nfsa_enrolled`, an any-of list and 7 exclusions. \"None of the any-of conditions\" → `needs_verification`. `ration_card_valid` is an external check.\n57 | - **Widow pension** mandatory docs include `bpl_proof`, all provisional (docs/schemes.md: \"commonly required; confirm locally\"). A DOB that is low-confidence, unreadable or missing → age `needs_verification`, never `not_eligible`.\n58 | - `RuleProvenance.sourceUrl` is nullable for provisional rules (needed for the T3 Orunodoi override \"provisional until an official notice URL is added\"). A schema refine stops a `verified` rule from having a null URL.\n59 | - `benefitOn`: overrides are inclusive date windows and the last match wins. `total` is null when `stateTopUp` is null.\n60 | - The registry is in-memory and keeps old versions. `getScheme(id)` returns the newest version; `getScheme(id, version)` returns that version.\n61 | \n62 | **Open issues**\n63 | - All Assamese strings (scheme questions, labels, check messages, rejection fix steps, tagline) are drafts and need native-speaker review (Das).\n64 | - The transliteration table is basic (no conjunct special cases beyond virama; schwa deletion only at word end).\n65 | - The registry test registers `nsap-widow@2.1.0` in the shared in-memory registry. Vitest isolates test files, so other files are unaffected.\n66 | \n67 | **Requests for Claude**\n68 | - Please confirm the readiness rule for external checks (they don't block `ready_for_review` on their own), or say if you want a different label, e.g. `ready_for_review` with a \"confirm these N items\" list. T2's UI will show them as a separate \"confirm at bank/portal\" group.\n69 | - Please confirm the Orunodoi any-of list and the widow pension `bpl_proof` document are wanted as modelled.\n70 | ","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\tasks\\backlog\\T2-main-flow.md","result":" 1 | # T2: Main flow end to end, API + UI (about 75 min)\n 2 | \n 3 | Mode: ACT. Mobile-first; **Assamese default, English toggle**; all fixed strings in `src/i18n.ts` (`as`, `en`). Use a font that renders Assamese well (e.g. Noto Sans Bengali, which covers Assamese).\n 4 | \n 5 | 1. `src/server/ai.ts` (the ONLY model caller): `extractDocument(imageBase64, hintDocType?)` → `ExtractedDoc` (zod), per-field confidence, one retry, safe fallback `{ error }`. Cline API (OpenAI-compatible) with image input; if images are rejected, note it under \"Requests for Claude\" and keep manual entry working. Mask Aadhaar inside ai.ts. Never store images.\n 6 | 2. `src/core/samples.ts`: samples A/B/C as in memory-bank/projectbrief.md (fake names, `XXXX XXXX 0000`-style Aadhaar).\n 7 | 3. API (`runtime = \"nodejs\"`): `POST /api/extract`, `POST /api/check` (schemeId, docs, answers, asOfDate? → Report).\n 8 | 4. UI steps: scheme cards (Assamese names; PM-KISAN marked \"flagship\") → documents (photo per mandatory doc, or \"Use sample A/B/C\") → confirm fields (low confidence highlighted) → yes/no questions (big buttons) → **report with TWO verdict banners**: \"Eligibility\" and \"Application readiness\", each 🟢/🔴/🟡/⚪ → check list (reason, where to fix, source link with \"verified on\" date, a \"provisional rule\" badge where relevant) → \"Print cover sheet\".\n 9 | 5. Footer on every report: \"We help catch preventable mistakes. We don't guarantee approval; the department decides.\" (Assamese + English).\n10 | \n11 | **Done when:** sample A → readiness ready_for_review with bank seeding flagged needs verification; sample B → action_required naming the land record and the bank name variant; sample C → action_required (death certificate); with AI unavailable, manual entry completes the flow; API tests (mocked ai.ts) pass; build passes; committed \"T2: main flow\".","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\PS.md","result":" 1 | # Cline AI Builder Hackathon: Round 2 Problem Statement\n 2 | \n 3 | India has problems that millions of people live with every day. What would you build with AI to solve one of them?\n 4 | \n 5 | India is building at a scale few countries have ever attempted, yet for hundreds of millions of people daily life still runs into the same walls. A farmer cannot tell what is wrong with his crop until the damage is done. A patient from a small town travels for hours to meet a doctor who has only a few minutes to give her. A student studies from notes written in a language she does not think in. A citizen loses months to a government scheme he qualified for but never heard about.\n 6 | \n 7 | These are not rare cases. They repeat across healthcare, education, agriculture, governance, finance, safety and climate, and across languages, incomes and literacy levels. AI can finally make a real dent: it understands Indian languages and voice, reads messy documents, reasons over local data and can reach anyone with a basic smartphone.\n 8 | \n 9 | **The challenge:** pick one real problem that Indian society faces and, in 8 hours, build an AI-powered solution for it, using Cline as your AI coding partner from the first commit to the last. You can also build Cline into the solution itself, for example with the Cline SDK. Not a slide deck, but a working product that a real person could use tomorrow.\n10 | \n11 | The problem is yours to choose. Healthcare, education, agriculture, governance, finance, safety and climate are only some examples, so look at the problems around you and pick one that matters. For example, potholes are a problem on roads across India, and one solution is a dashcam in a car with AI that spots potholes as it drives and prepares the complaint automatically.\n12 | \n13 | ## Deliverables\n14 | - **Codebase on GitHub (with README):** a public repository with a clear README covering the problem, your solution, architecture, tech stack, setup steps and how Cline was used in the build.\n15 | - **PPT:** a presentation covering the problem, your solution, the architecture, the AI models and tools involved, how Cline was used (in the build and inside the solution), challenges faced and future scope.\n16 | - **Demo video (mandatory):** a short walkthrough of your working solution with a real user scenario, showing Cline in action during the build.\n17 | - **Social media post (brownie points):** share your build, demo, experience or participation shoutout, and tag Cline.\n18 | \n19 | ## Evaluation criteria\n20 | Creativity & uniqueness · Innovation · Real-world usefulness · Effective use of Cline · Product usability & overall execution · Technical implementation. **Bonus** for solutions that use Cline inside the product itself, not only to build it.","success":true},{"query":"C:\\Dev\\cline hackathon\\build\\docs\\README.md","result":"1 | # docs/\n2 | - `PS.md`: the Round 2 problem statement (owned by Claude and the user; Cline does not edit).\n3 | - `research.md`: evidence and pitch for README and slides.\n4 | - `schemes.md`: **rule packs v2**, the source of truth for the rule engine (provenance, verified vs provisional).\n5 | - `sample-guideline-ignoaps.md`: demo input for the Rule Maintenance Agent (add a new scheme).\n6 | - `sample-notice-orunodoi-oct2026.md`: demo input for the Rule Maintenance Agent (a versioned temporary change).","success":true}],"durationMs":20}}
