with dynamic params, also follow the \r\n[`generateStaticParams`](#generatestaticparams-and-dynamicparams) guidance. Routes that still render instantly need no further work.\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:102:4. **Convert one route at a time.** Remove `instant = false` from a route, then resolve its insights by caching data with [`use \r\ncache`](/docs/app/api-reference/directives/use-cache) or wrapping runtime data in [`<Suspense>`](https://react.dev/reference/react/Suspense). Repeat until no routes opt out.\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:136:## `dynamic = \"force-dynamic\"`\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:138:**Remove the config.** Without Cache Components, `dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` rendered the entire route for every request and made its `fetch` requests uncached. With \r\nCache Components, uncached data and [Request-time APIs](/docs/app/glossary#request-time-apis) already run at request time. Next.js prerenders any static or cached UI around them.\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:144:export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:153:export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:174:## `dynamic = \"force-static\"`\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:176:**Remove the config, then make its caching explicit.** Without Cache Components, `dynamic = 'force-static'` forced the route to prerender, cached its data, and made \r\n`cookies()`, `headers()`, and `useSearchParams()` return empty values.\r\nnode_modules\\next\\dist\\docs\\01-app\\02-guides\\migrating-to-cache-components.md:182:export const dynamic = 'force-static'\r\nnode_modules\\next\