{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:46:54.184Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm reconsidering whether to pass all samples to the docs step or filter them to only those matching the currently selected scheme, since showing unrelated samples like one for a widow's case under PM-KISAN would be confusing — I'll filter samples by scheme for clarity.\n\nNow moving to ConfirmStep: I need to render fields per document type with editable inputs, using local draft state keyed by docType and field so typing numbers like Aadhaar's last-4 digits doesn't get mangled by the parsing logic. I'm restricting the Aadhaar input to 4 digits with numeric input mode to avoid collecting full Aadhaar numbers, and handling the DOB field as plain text to sidestep date-input locale issues.\n\nI'm also reconsidering which fields to actually collect per document — for minimal data, I decide to drop husbandName from death_certificate entirely since it's not used by the eligibility engine, only the document's presence matters, and similarly for bpl_proof fields not referenced by the rules for a given scheme.\n\nNow I'm sketching out the UI components: QuestionsStep with Yes/No toggle buttons and provisional badges, ReportStep handling idle/loading/error/done states with eligibility and readiness banners, fix/verify sections, supporting docs, and print/start-over controls. For CheckItem I'm planning the message display, fix location, source link with verification date, provisional badge, and name match score.\n\nI'm also designing a print-only CoverSheet (hidden on screen, visible via print:block) showing title, scheme, verdicts, masked Aadhaar docs, fix/verify lists, and disclaimer in the current language. For page.tsx, I'm making it a server component that builds the catalog from listSchemes() and SAMPLES and renders KaagazApp, which should work fine as a static page since there's no dynamic data involved. One tradeoff I'm accepting is that importing the Report zod schema and ExtractedDoc types into client components pulls zod into the client bundle, which is acceptable here.\n\nNow I'll move on to writing the remaining files.\n\nI'll stop reading the husband's name and BPL proof name since the engine never uses them, then filter the samples to the chosen scheme.\n\n"}}
