{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:49:47.632Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"The end-to-end run worked correctly with samples A/B/C and graceful fallback when AI is unavailable. But I'm puzzled why .env.local shows the key is set while the app reports it unavailable with a null model—possibly `next start` isn't loading .env.local the same way, or there's a formatting issue like quotes or whitespace in the variable despite my check confirming it's set.\n\nI'm questioning whether process.env is being accessed correctly at runtime, since Next.js only inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables at build time, so server-side process.env access should still work normally. The server log didn't show the expected \"Environments: .env.local\" line, which makes me suspect the file might not be loading at all—possibly due to encoding issues like UTF-16 if it was written via PowerShell, which could throw off Next's env parsing even though standard file reading tools handle it fine.\n\nSamples A, B, and C work as expected via the real HTTP API, but the gateway reports `model: null` at runtime despite `.env.local` having both keys set. I'll check the file's encoding and line format (without printing values) to find why they aren't being picked up.\n\n"}}
