{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:49:58.295Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"I'm puzzled why Node's loadEnvFile picks up the key but not the model variable—checking for line-ending issues or something odd in how the CLINE_MODEL line is parsed, since the regex seems to match the key correctly.\n\nNo BOM at the file start, so I'm wondering if there's a hidden character like a zero-width char in the key name causing the mismatch. Since Next.js logs show the model as null, meaning the config resolution failed, I want to print the character codes of the key to check for anything invisible.\n\nTurns out `.env.local` exists after all, despite NEXT.md saying otherwise — Node picks up `CLINE_API_KEY` but not `CLINE_MODEL`. I'll inspect the key names' character codes without exposing any values.\n\n"}}
