{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:50:17.348Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"Found it — this terminal has CLINE_MODEL set to an empty string as an env var, which overrides .env.local since Next won't override existing env vars, so the server sees it as empty and falls back to ai_unavailable. That's just a quirk of this shell session, not a real bug, and it actually demonstrates the graceful fallback working correctly. I could restart the server with that variable removed to test against the real model.\n\nDoing a real test makes sense since it'll send a trivial 1x1 image (no personal data, negligible cost) just to check whether image input is accepted at all, which answers the requirement to note if images get rejected — it probably won't return useful extracted fields but at least confirms 200 vs 400. I'll stop the current server first to do this cleanly.\n\nFound it: an empty `CLINE_MODEL` env var is overriding `.env.local`, causing the fallback behavior. I'll restart the server without that variable and send a 1×1 test image to check if the Cline API accepts image input.\n\n"}}
