{"ts":"2026-10-10T09:52:12.714Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"The smoke test passes end to end, and I confirm the lint ran after all UI files were written, so KaagazApp's React hooks rules check out fine. I'll still rerun the full suite after the changes to be safe.\n\nI should verify the smoke script's .mjs extension doesn't trip up tsconfig or lint—it's excluded from TS includes but still lintable, so I'll rerun lint to confirm. Checking sample data: bpl_proof's name field stays in the doc even though it's not displayed, which is fine, and since sample confidences are ≥0.8 nothing gets highlighted, which is acceptable to leave as-is since I shouldn't tweak samples just for demo effect. The Orunodoi scheme has no sample so it stays manual-only. Next I'll run test, typecheck, lint, and build, check git status for stray files, then update the log and memory bank before committing.\n\nI want to note two gotchas: Next 16 with cacheComponents rejects the `runtime = \"nodejs\"` export, and the shell's empty CLINE_MODEL env var shadows .env.local since Next's env loader won't override existing keys even if empty—this is an environment issue to document rather than code around. I also confirm the Cline API's image capability works fine, and the requirement to log model, prompt version, and input hash is satisfied. Now I'll proceed with the final checks.\n\n"}}
